All panel dialog demos on the CSS docs page rendered as fullscreen dialogs (full viewport width) instead of the expected 384px-wide side panel.

## Root cause

`src/tags/site-header/style.scss` contained an unscoped `@media (min-width: 512px)` rule that clobbered `@ebay/skin`'s `width: 384px` for every `.panel-dialog__window` on the page:

```scss
/* Before — matches ALL panel dialogs on the page */
@media (min-width: 512px) {
  .panel-dialog__window {
    width: 100%;
  }
}
```

This was intentional for the site's own mobile nav panel, but leaked globally due to the unscoped selector.

## Fix

Scope the override to the mobile nav panel's own class:

```scss
/* After — only affects the site header's mobile nav panel */
@media (min-width: 512px) {
  .site-nav-mobile-panel .panel-dialog__window {
    width: 100%;
  }
}
```

The pass direction buttons (← left, → right) were mapped backwards in game logic. Each player station is CSS-rotated to face center, so visually ← points counterclockwise and → points clockwise — but the code had it inverted.

### Changes in `src/engine/gameEngine.ts`

- **`getPassTarget`**: Swapped `left → clockwise` to `left → counterclockwise` (and vice versa)
- **`passAction` expectedDir**: Clockwise play now expects `'right'` button press, not `'left'`
- **`decideAIAction`**: All AI pass direction choices updated to match corrected mapping

```typescript
// Before (wrong): "pass left" = clockwise
const dir: Direction = passDirection === 'left' ? 'clockwise' : 'counterclockwise';

// After (correct): "pass left" = counterclockwise
const dir: Direction = passDirection === 'left' ? 'counterclockwise' : 'clockwise';
```
